Three months later, a fire broke out in her friend's boutique, causing damage worth ₹10 lakhs.
Priya approached the insurance company to claim the amount, stating that she had paid the
premium regularly and held a valid insurance policy for that boutique.
However, the insurance company rejected her claim, even though she had a proper policy and
had paid the premium on time.
